# Canonical text checkout.
#
# Recorded artifact digests (artifact/v1) are SHA-256 over the exact bytes on
# disk. Without a normalisation rule a Windows CRLF checkout hashes differently
# from a Linux LF checkout, so the same commit fails `workflow verify` and
# tests/test_example_artifacts.py on one platform or the other. Forcing LF for
# text makes checkouts byte-stable everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Declare binaries explicitly so auto-detection never rewrites them (a PNG can
# legitimately contain a CRLF byte pair inside compressed data).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.whl binary
